  "m_sweep": {
    "_provenance": "msweep2.py, N=64, care radius h=2, fan-in = min(max(16,4M),20), yosys 0.33, same settings as cam_baseline.py.",
    "_caveat": "h=2 (rather than the h=3 used elsewhere) FAVOURS the HNN: fewer care rows -> fewer terms -> less area. The CAM is unaffected by h. So the HNN's losses here are conservative. The fan-in cap of 20 is an espresso-runtime limit and is what breaks storage at M>=8; lifting it would restore storage but at exponentially more area.",
