    "finding_1_design_rule": "Scheduling delays MUST exceed worst-case combinational propagation delay through the neuron's SOP. At scale=1 the gate delays (1-5ns each over several levels, ~20-30ns total) dominate the scheduling delays (1-7ns), so commits are sequenced on stale logic and the colouring is meaningless. This is a design-rule violation, not a hazard effect, and it accounted for most of the damage: agreement 50% -> 90% simply by scaling the schedule.",
    "finding_2_residual_hazards": "After the design rule is satisfied the effect saturates at 90% agreement and 90% recall vs 95% behavioural. It does not improve from scale=20 to scale=100, which is the signature of a hazard rather than a timing shortfall. So hazards are real but small: ~5 percentage points of recall, ~10% of inputs reaching a different fixed point.",
